				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">He stretched out a little, Solusek Ro had just been slain, and he was preparing himself for his first venture into Doomfire on his own when A voice boomed through the air.  It spoke of Terris Thule, and a war.  He didn't pay much attention, it had nothing to do with him.  
<br />

<br />
"So you guys are at war now eh?" He said
<br />

<br />
"Yeah, this is gonna suck" She replied
<br />

<br />
"So where are you?" He asked, a bit of concern in his voice.
<br />

<br />
"We just wiped, we were doing an adventure in Everfrost"
<br />

<br />
"Wiped eh?  I'll be there in a minute or so"  With that he mounted his proud war steed Bill Jr, and made for the snowy peaks of everfrost.  Bill Jr's speed and endurence made the trip quite enjoyable.  
<br />

<br />
As he approched the forgotten tower in Everfrost, he felt a slight pinching sensation on his behind, it was a familiar feeling, and a welcome one.  He entered the tower, only to see her slain body on the gound.
<br />

<br />
'Need a rez eh?" He said, laying on the sarcasm pretty thick.
<br />

<br />
"Yeah, cleric is inc though, shouldn't be long."  She replied, seeming quite unconcerned with all that was going on around her.
<br />

<br />
"Well after you get that rez, get some mana back, do some quick buffs, then get the hell out of here, don't want nothing bad happening to ya."  He said, placing his hand on the handle of his sword.
<br />

<br />
The two sat in the snow waiting for the arrival of the cleric, she was day dreaming, he sat quietly, keeping a vigilant watch of all that was around him.  Upon the clerics arrival, she regained her lost experience, and began to prepare herself for travel, readying herself for the worst.
<br />

<br />
"Make it quick," He said "I don't think we've got much time left befo..."
<br />

<br />
As he spoke, he saw a warrior, native to the mountians and frozen plains, advancing.
<br />

<br />
"Gah, get SoE up, and get the hell out of here"  He yelled. 
<br />

<br />
The warrior drew his sword, and quickly made his way tward her.
<br />

<br />
"Don't touch her." He yelled at the warrior, but had no effect, he pounded his sword tward her with a seemingly inhuman speed, deeply slicing her arm.
<br />

<br />
He drew his sword, and leaped at the attacking warrior, "I said don't touch her!"  He screamed, his eyes burned with an intense hatered, his muscles bulged, his body moved with grace and simplicity, as if it was not him moving, but the air around him, twisting and contorting to his will.
<br />

<br />
"Get the hell out of here, NOW!"  He howled, his was gritty and deep, not at all his own.  She ran as fast as her spirit, and feet could take her.
<br />

<br />
He swung at the warrior, as his sword drew near the warrior's chest, he felt something come over him, his vision blurred, and he slipped into darkness.
<br />

<br />
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<br />

<br />
He pounded his desk.
<br />

<br />
"FUCK!" he shouted, his sister entered the room.
<br />

<br />
"What happened?" she asked, looking a bit concerned.
<br />

<br />
"I'm kos to Wudan." he grumbled.
<br />

<br />
"Wudan? As in the guild that you applied to, and have been working at for the last 6 months Wudan?" she asked, looking suprised.
<br />

<br />
"Yup." He said sharply.
<br />

<br />
"Damn, that sucks, what happened?" she asked.
<br />

<br />
"Long story, doesn't really matter now though." he said, a bit of despair slipped through in his voice.
<br />

<br />
"Well it still sucks." she responded, trying to sympathize
<br />

<br />
